   "evidence": "New file declares `integrable_fourier_mul_conj_fourier {X Y : \u03a9 \u2192 AddCircle T}` in `EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Analysis/Fourier/AddCircle.lean`; the expectation of the same product is declared at `EpsilonEridani/Nuclear/Medium/Collective/Basic.lean:362`. Its proof uses only `IndepFun.integral_fun_comp_mul_comp` (upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Probability/Independence/Integration.lean:380), `integral_conj` and `HasLaw.integral_comp` \u2014 no declaration from this roadmap \u2014 and the PR description states it is generalised to two laws for a future \u00a75.3 use rather than for the \u00a75.1 statement proved here.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Nuclear/Medium/Collective/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Move it to `EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Analysis/Fourier/AddCircle.lean` next to `integrable_fourier_mul_conj_fourier`, stated in integral form (no `anisotropyCoeff`), and use it in `integral_norm_qVector_sq` after `anisotropyCoeff_def`; do not keep an `anisotropyCoeff`-phrased restatement in Collective, since `anisotropyCoeff \u03bc n` is by definition `\u222b x, fourier n x \u2202\u03bc` and that would be a duplicate. The move needs only `Mathlib.Probability.Independence.Integration` (and `Mathlib.Probability.HasLaw`, or phrase it with `P.map X`) added to that file, which already fixes `{\u03a9} [MeasurableSpace \u03a9] {P} [IsFiniteMeasure P]`.",
   "issue": "`integral_fourier_mul_conj_fourier` contains nothing nuclear: it is the statement that for independent circle-valued `X, Y` with laws `\u03bc, \u03bd`, `E[fourier n X * conj (fourier n Y)] = (\u222b fourier n \u2202\u03bc) * conj (\u222b fourier n \u2202\u03bd)`. Its integrability companion for the very same expression, `integrable_fourier_mul_conj_fourier`, was put in the generic `Mathematics/Analysis/Fourier/AddCircle.lean`, so the generic result is the one buried in a Layer-5 physics module where unrelated harmonic work will not find it.",
   "line": "362"
  }
